<title>USA: Cytec Industries Q1 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Cytec Industries Q1 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>WEST PATERSON, N.J. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Tables to Follow -0-</p>
<p>		   CYTEC INDUSTRIES INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>			CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME</p>
<p>(Millions of dollars, except share and per share amounts)</p>
<p>							  Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								     March 31,</p>
<p>							  1997	    1996</p>
<p>Net sales					  $ 306.5  +1%  $ 304.5</p>
<p>Manufacturing cost of sale		     235.0	   217.6</p>
<p>Selling and technical services		  34.6	    34.9</p>
<p>Research and process development		10.3	    10.3</p>
<p>Administrative and general			11.0	    11.1</p>
<p>Earnings from operations			  15.6	    30.6</p>
<p>Other income (expense), net		     24.4	     1.3</p>
<p>Equity in earnings of associated companies   4.5	     6.6</p>
<p>Interest income (expense), net		 (0.2)	   (0.5)</p>
<p>Earnings before income taxes		    44.3	    38.0</p>
<p>Income tax provision				17.4	    15.4</p>
<p>Net earnings				     $  26.9	 $  22.6</p>
<p>Earnings per common share			$0.56  +27%   $0.44</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding (including  </p>
<p>   common stock equivalents)	    47,876,000    51,188,000</p>
<p>27 Percent</p>
<p>NOTE: Certain reclassifications have been made to the consolidated statement of Income for the three month period ended March 31, 1996, to conform to the 1997 presentation. They are as follows:</p>
<p>-- Equity in earnings of associated companies is now shown before the taxes on the company's share of income from such companies whereas in 1996 and prior it was shown net of tax.</p>
<p>-- The income tax provision has been adjusted to include the taxes attributable to the company's share of earnings from associated companies.</p>
<p>-- Other income (expense), net does not include interest income which is now included as part of interest expense, net.</p>
<p>-- Only one earnings per share calculation is shown as dilution in earnings per share from all potential dilution is less than three percent of primary earnings per share.</p>
